#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# algebraic_number_trace

#% text
# `algebraic_number_trace(a)` gives the trace of the algebraic number `a` over the rational numbers: the sum of its conjugates, computed in the field Q(a).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is read off the minimal polynomial: for `x^n + c(n-1) x^(n-1) + ... + c0` the norm is `(-1)^n c0` and the trace `-c(n-1)`.

#% item
# A rational number has itself as norm and trace.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
algebraic_number_trace(1 + sqrt(2))
#% output
#= 2

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
algebraic_number_trace(2^(1/3) + 1)
#% output
#= 3

#% cell
algebraic_number_trace(sqrt(2) + sqrt(3))
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
algebraic_number_trace(root(x => x^5 - x - 1, 2))
#% output
#= 0

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The values come from the minimal polynomial:

#% cell
minimal_polynomial(2^(1/3) + 1, x)
#% output
#= -3 + 3*x - 3*x^2 + x^3

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `algebraic_number_norm`, `minimal_polynomial`, `root_reduce`
